{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-72644",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{(-2)^{7}}{(-2)^{3}} \\\\  & =(-2)^{7}÷(-2)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{7}÷(-2)^{3} & =(-2)^{7-3} \\\\  & =(-2)^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
